WEBVTT

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:04.690
This is it.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.320
Welcome.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:56.840
Order: Piciformes
Family: Picidae
Genus: Colaptes

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:50.270
Welcome to Lodge Campo.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.720
Will you be staying the night?

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:53.370
Yeah!

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:56.840
Then please pick out your room first.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.610
It's like we're walking inside a tree!

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:02.300
It's pretty tall.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:07.560
This facility was built long, long ago. 
I've repurposed it as a lodge.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:12.660
This is the Floaty Room.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.930
The feeling of being rocked 
to sleep in a hammock

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:18.490
is popular with Friends 
who live underwater.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:19.780
Wow!

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:24.460
For Friends who like dark places, 
we have the Quiet Room.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:26.890
It's moderately moist, moderately dark,

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:30.530
and best of all, the closeness 
of the walls is calming.

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:31.330
Really?

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:35.410
This is our orthodox View Room.

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:37.000
In the daytime, you have a wide view.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.680
You can unwind with the feeling 
of sleeping in a real treetop.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:46.070
They're all so great, it's hard to choose.

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:49.600
You love your rooms, don't you, 
Campo Flicker-san?

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:52.360
We'll take this room! It has a great view.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.170
Understood. Make yourselves at home.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:56.900
Hey, Kaban-chan, let's explore 
after we bring our stuff in.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:57.860
Yeah.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.630
Not sleepy today?

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:06.540
Yeah.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.560
What an interesting design.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.790
You can go to the neighboring trees, too!

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.270
What'cha doing?

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:19.590
You came in at just the right moment.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:24.350
Order: Carnivora
Family: Canidae
Genus: Canis

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:24.350
I'm Gray Wolf, an author. 
I'm working on a rough draft right now.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.050
What's this? What's this?

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:30.100
It looks a lot like a book.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.520
You know your stuff.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:37.190
This is called "manga." I'm asking 
the professor to turn it into a book.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:41.970
Anyway, you two must be pretty 
fearless if you're staying here.

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:42.610
Huh?

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:46.360
This lodge is famous for being haunted.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:51.250
If you sleep here, you'll see a 
purple Cerulean in your dreams...

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:56.030
If that Cerulean eats you in your dream,

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:59.050
you'll be stuck in your dream forever.

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:04.300
Thanks for the great expressions!

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:05.400
Huh?

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:09.210
Just kidding. It's not true.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:11.270
This is a peaceful lodge.

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:15.510
I get some good material by telling 
guests scary stories like this.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:16.810
You scared me!

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.860
That's so mean! She scared us for real!

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:25.160
I'm still scared after what she said...

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.830
Order: Artiodactyla
Family: Giraffidae
Genus: Giraffa

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.830
Oh, my. Who are you?

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.750
Nice to meet you! I'm—

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.690
Wait! I'll deduce it.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:41.420
Your outfit... an affinity for 
climbing high up trees... the time...

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:47.150
From this evidence, 
your species is obvious to me.

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:49.510
You are... a goat!

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.200
That's not even close!

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:58.270
Strange... I, the Great Detective 
Giraffe, could never be wrong.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:00.730
You're lying about something, aren't you?

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.870
Huh? That's crazy.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:05.580
I'm Serval. It's true!

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:09.740
Your desperate denial only makes you
more suspicious. Now confess!

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:11.940
That was an awful experience.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:14.870
She was a unique Friend.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:20.870
The usual again?

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:24.660
Hello! Today we came to the lodge.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:29.550
Here, you can watch animals from the treetops 
and stay the night with Friends.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:30.830
The lodge...

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:34.270
So Mirai-san has been here before, too.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:39.440
It's so sparkly clean. We're busy dealing 
with the Cerulean outbreak right now,

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:44.280
but our efforts to get ready to reopen 
the park are coming along, too.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.010
Well, until next time!

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:49.760
Huh? Something's wrong 
with the "stop" button.

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:54.380
Is it because it got wet in that rain?

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:05.940
Good morning.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.630
Morning!

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:11.930
What's up?

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.610
Good morning.

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:17.100
I saw something strange yesterday...

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.460
Something strange?

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:21.750
I was making my rounds around the lodge 
to turn out the lights, like I always do,

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.590
when I saw a strange shadow.

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:30.150
When I walked closer to call out to them, 
they ran away at an unbelievable speed.

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:32.950
Do you two know anything?

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:36.880
No. I could never run that fast.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.260
I think I'm pretty fast!

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:42.960
But I didn't run around yesterday.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:50.340
Of course... At that time, all of the 
guests were in a different place...

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:55.260
Supposedly there are Ceruleans 
that can move at high speeds.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:58.000
They're faster than any Friends.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.350
You can run and run, 
but you'll never shake them.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:03.270
Until finally... they gobble you up!

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:06.850
Do you know what happens to the 
girls who are eaten by Ceruleans?

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:09.330
There's no escaping from inside them.

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:11.600
First, your whole body melts away...

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:15.090
Goodness! Wolf-san!

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:16.570
Just kidding.

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:18.620
I got some good expressions again.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:23.960
B-Be it a Cerulean or a Friend, 
we must get to the bottom of this!

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:26.960
I'll just have to do my best!

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:31.180
There might be some clues. 
Let's go to the scene of the crime!

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:38.640
It was there. I saw it on that branch.

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:41.760
It seemed pretty big.

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:45.310
And then, in the next instant, 
it moved over to that tree.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.700
Sounds like a Cerulean.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:51.950
It didn't smell much like one, though.

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.550
It must be a red Cerulean!

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.970
I'll go make the rounds, just to be safe.

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:02.040
I'm so sorry for the fuss.

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:05.660
Think it's about time we headed out?

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:13.480
Stormy weather incoming today.

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:18.090
The road ahead is unstable. To be safe, 
we should leave after the rain stops.

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:18.800
Oh, really?

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:21.550
Well, we'll be staying a little longer, then.

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:24.060
Okay! We're happy to have you!

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:57.590
Japan Wolf Association, Nanbu-oneesan (Shizuoka)

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:32.490
They have slender, long legs,
and a body like a marathon runner.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:37.570
Their palms and soles of their feet, to put 
it in human terms, are particularly big.

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:43.010
The wolf is a traveling animal. They patrol 
their territory and hunt every day.

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:47.900
Their paws have to be big for that, 
and they're built to run efficiently.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:51.730
They're cowardly and nervous and cautious, 
but they're also curious.

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:57.590
Communication is a part of their daily 
lives, so they're very expressive.

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:00.320
They look like they have two horns,

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:27.400
Tobu Zoo, Yamakami-oniisan (Saitama)

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:03.520
but on their brows, they have a lump 
that is actually another "horn."

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:08.040
And behind the ears, there are two 
more bumps, so that's five in all.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:11.630
They're typically high-strung and nervous.

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:15.960
If they hear something, 
or see something strange or new,

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:18.280
they'll stiffen up and won't budge.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:22.220
In the light and shade of trees, they blend 
in with their surroundings, like leopards.

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:27.620
As calves, they'll sit in the shade 
and hide in the brush.

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:34.170
Kaban-san is incredible. She even 
saved the hot spring from disaster?

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:37.920
Anyway, we got permission 
from the professor,

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:42.860
so now we're going after the treasure 
and chasing down the thief.

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:44.520
Very interesting.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:47.700
Do you think it has anything to do 
with the recent Cerulean outbreak?

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:51.200
You're gonna need to bring some 
pretty rare items, or you'll end up dead.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:54.230
There you go, talking about 
video games again...

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:16.420
Serval-chan?

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:32.290
Where'd Serval-chan go?

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:35.940
But really, at any rate...

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:42.640
O-Oh, it's you... You scared me.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:47.140
A complete evacuation would be overreacting. 
We don't need to go <i>that</i> far...

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:51.260
We'll be okay, but Mirai-san, 
you and your friends need to hide!

00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:56.030
This is too sudden. We need to find some way 
to keep the park peaceful forever...

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:59.520
Huh? It's recording again?

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:05.730
This is completely broken... 
I'll waterproof it later.

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:08.910
What a cutie! What's it for?

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:12.910
One day, this will be used as a park guide...

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:18.070
P-Please don't eat me!

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:19.190
I won't ea—

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:21.110
I-I'm not eating anything!

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:24.750
Serval-chan? Where were you?

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:29.250
Um, I was just, uh... 
Right, I went for a walk!

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:32.600
This time, Giraffe-san saw it.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:34.000
What?!

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.660
Are you okay?

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:37.240
What was it like?

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:39.710
It was white and hazy.

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:41.990
It didn't feel alive.

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:45.210
This is a paranormal mystery.

00:11:45.210 --> 00:11:48.200
I still think it must be a Cerulean...

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:51.880
But are there any white, hazy Ceruleans?

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:55.650
Well, sometimes you hear about new types.

00:11:55.650 --> 00:12:02.450
Its silhouette was the same shape 
as a Friend... That was terrifying.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:06.540
So there really is someone here?

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:09.340
Who is it? It's not you again, is it, Wolf-san?

00:12:09.340 --> 00:12:11.030
It's not me.

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:14.040
Maybe someone's hiding in the 
forest and playing a prank?

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.190
Have you heard this story?

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:20.130
Supposedly, long ago, there was 
a Friend-shaped Cerulean.

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:22.540
Huh? Can you tell the difference at a glance?

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:27.230
If you can't... you might think they're a Friend, 
approach them, and be eaten...

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:29.240
Scary, scary, scary!

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:31.810
Well, I don't know about that.

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:34.070
But the terrifying part 
about this story is that,

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:36.730
supposedly, the Cerulean itself 
didn't know what it was...

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:42.220
In other words, you might think that 
you're a Friend, but the truth is,

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:45.200
you might be a Cerulean, too!

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:48.600
That's scarier, scarier, scarier!

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:51.400
I'm kidding. Got some good expressions.

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:54.160
I hope it's only a prank, but...

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:58.500
We should be extra careful, and avoid 
being alone as much as possible.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.340
The rain still isn't letting up.

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:08.760
Let's explore the lodge again!

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:15.070
I think Boss is about to say something again!

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:21.150
I know. Since it's malfunctioning anyway, 
I'll use it to take notes!

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:26.990
Friends are born when Sandstar 
reacts with "living creatures"

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:28.770
or "the remains of living creatures."

00:13:28.770 --> 00:13:32.950
We've now learned that Ceruleans are born 
when it reacts with "inorganic material."

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.300
However, in other research,

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:37.920
it's been hypothesized that there may 
be more than one type of Sandstar.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:42.960
That's something else to consider. End memo.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:45.430
It's too hard to really understand, huh?

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:48.720
Do you think the professor and her 
assistant would like to hear about this?

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:51.690
I dunno. It doesn't have 
anything to do with food...

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:56.310
I'll tell them about it when I go report 
to them after finding your territory.

00:13:56.770 --> 00:14:01.160
If the port and the ocean really do
turn out to be your territory,

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:02.690
what will you do next?

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:04.540
Well...

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:09.050
If there are humans there, 
I'd like to ask them how humans live.

00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:10.530
If there aren't...

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:12.990
I'll think about it.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:16.870
If you end up living by the seaside, 
come visit me in the savanna, too!

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:23.000
Or would you want to live together, 
like Beaver and Prairie Dog? Seems fun!

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:28.840
Huh? At first, you thought I was an alien?!

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:34.250
We didn't know there were any 
Areas outside of our island!

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:36.750
Besides, you came flying in.

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:39.460
Some of us thought you'd eat us.

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:42.610
I'm an alien!

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:46.430
Welcome to the labyrinth!

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:50.760
Sounds like a fun time!

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:53.910
Mirai-san must be a great person, right?

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:58.500
Are you okay?

00:14:58.500 --> 00:14:59.790
What happened?

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:03.250
Just now... the white ghost 
was right there...

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.250
Trying to scare us again?

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:06.910
We're not falling for that anymore!

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:09.140
No, I'm not! This time I'm telling the truth!

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:10.660
There you go again!

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:14.100
Serval-chan, she's acting 
different this time.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:17.400
It was definitely white... and it had 
the same shape as a Friend...

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:19.660
It had either ears or horns.

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:21.850
And it was a lot bigger than I'd heard.

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:24.550
About as tall as that tree.

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:26.150
That's way too big!

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:28.520
Maybe there are multiple kinds?

00:15:28.520 --> 00:15:31.610
Um, so far there were...

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:34.690
Campo-san saw it two nights ago.
Giraffe did last night.

00:15:34.690 --> 00:15:35.910
And I did just now.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.170
Is it always at night?

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:38.140
Yeah.

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:41.370
It was a different thing in 
a different place each time...

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:44.920
There has to be someone else here.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:48.890
I don't hear or smell any other Friends nearby.

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:52.130
Someone could be lying and pulling a prank.

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:53.890
Then it would be you, Wolf!

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:56.510
I've never told a lie.

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:58.340
Oh, really?

00:15:58.340 --> 00:16:00.290
Horns or ears...

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:04.330
Let's try talking about it tomorrow, 
when everyone's together again.

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:04.760
Okay.

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:05.860
Okay!

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:10.640
Oh, yes... Speaking of ear shapes, 
on the night of a full moon, wolves will...

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:12.950
Hey! There you go again!

00:16:14.920 --> 00:16:16.720
Morning, Serval-chan.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.220
You can keep sleeping, you know.

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:20.700
Morning...

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:24.720
The sky cleared up! 
Looks like we can leave today.

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:25.710
Yeah.

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:31.800
P-Please don't eat me!

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:33.030
Gh-Ghost!

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:35.280
Let's run, Kaban-chan!

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:38.760
Serval-chan, I'm scared too, 
but let's at least get a better look at it.

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:40.810
We might find a clue.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:46.080
They were right. It's shaped like a Friend.

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:47.900
It has ears...

00:16:56.540 --> 00:16:58.660
We saw it, too.

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:08.220
No matter how many times we go over it, 
I don't think anyone's lying.

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:10.630
Has anyone noticed any other unusual things?

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:14.800
Now that you mention it, there have been 
Japari buns disappearing overnight.

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:17.300
Wh-Wh-Who could have done that?

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:21.210
Oh, that was just Serval-chan. 
I don't think it's related.

00:17:21.210 --> 00:17:23.790
Kaban-chan, how'd you know?

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:26.120
It has to be a Cerulean, right?

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:29.390
But you said it had ears and 
was shaped like a Friend.

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:31.570
Could be a new humanoid kind.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:34.650
Even a Cerulean would have 
a scent or make noise, right?

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:37.530
If I was a Cerulean...

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:40.410
Wait... huh?

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.260
U-Um...

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:44.450
I've got it!

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:45.530
The culprit is...

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:46.760
Wolf-san!

00:17:46.760 --> 00:17:48.540
What?!

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:53.200
Wolf-san did this in the hopes that it 
would get her manga talked about.

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:56.880
A pitiful motive from an unknown author!

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:59.550
Uh... Motive aside...

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:02.390
How is she making a ghost appear?

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:04.290
They're twins!

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:08.080
They have the same scent. 
That's why we didn't realize!

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:11.620
That doesn't explain how fast 
it was or how big it was.

00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:14.440
So my twin is white and see-through?

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:16.030
It's possible if you're triplets!

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:18.410
No, quadruplets, even!

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:20.360
C-Calm down, Giraffe-san.

00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:21.980
You're getting too heated up.

00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:25.040
Um, I might have figured it out.

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:27.540
The culprit is...

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:34.450
me.

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:36.760
What?!

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:39.060
What do you mean, Kaban-san?

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:40.730
Don't tell me, you can transform?

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:42.410
You're kidding, right, Kaban-chan?

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:44.520
I mean, we were together this morning!

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:48.340
Er... I think you'll understand 
once you see it.

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:50.520
Walk with me for a bit.

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:58.400
The ghost seemed to appear in different 
places, but I was always nearby.

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:00.920
And most of all, every time...

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:12.670
It was in a place where we had 
listened to Mirai-san's messages.

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:19.220
Lucky-san was making it 
appear where I walked.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:20.550
I'm sorry for upsetting you.

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:22.460
Wh-What is this?

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:24.850
I've never seen anything like it.

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:28.270
Things aren't looking good.

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:29.280
This is...

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:30.890
She's Mirai-san?

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:33.080
Yeah. She has to be.

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:35.170
Is that the lodge?

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:37.390
It's so shiny and new.

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:40.900
What the... Did Boss 
swallow it up, time and all?

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:43.070
You're saying scary things again...

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:47.340
That Cerulean is huge, 
but the real problem is that,

00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:50.600
no matter how much we chip away 
at it, it always heals itself.

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:54.420
If we can't defeat it this week, 
we'll have to leave the park...

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:55.790
What's that about?

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:58.780
She's talking about something scary.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:04.130
Well... Honestly, I wanted 
to stay on this island longer...

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:05.850
I never thought it might be over so soon...

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:07.230
Mirai-san!

00:20:07.230 --> 00:20:08.770
Hurry, hurry!

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:11.790
Caracal says she saw the 
big one at the mountain!

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:14.150
Let's all work together to take it down!

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:15.950
Huh?

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:19.950
Yes, you're right. If we finish it off now,
everything will be resolved.

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:21.590
Let's go in like "boom"!

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:24.160
Yeah! Boom!

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:26.400
Was that... you, Serval-chan?

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:29.460
I don't remember that. 
I think it's another serval.

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:32.960
I guess sometimes there are multiple 
Friends from the same species, so...

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:38.510
Huh? What?

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:41.510
Huh? That's weird.

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:43.370
Is it because I got up early?

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:47.800
I got some good material.

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:51.880
Is that Horror Detective Girogiro?!

00:20:51.880 --> 00:20:55.650
R-Reading that is what inspired 
me to become a detective!

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:57.370
Can I have your autograph?!

00:20:59.870 --> 00:21:01.090
The bus is departing.

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:02.520
See you again.

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:04.960
Please stop by again sometime, okay?

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:06.190
See you.

00:21:06.190 --> 00:21:07.300
See ya.

00:21:09.020 --> 00:21:11.080
So this is the ocean.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:14.010
A boat! That has to be a boat, right?

00:21:14.010 --> 00:21:15.540
Wow!

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:17.990
Hello? Anyone here?

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:20.210
Looks like there aren't any humans here.

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:22.710
Maybe this was the wrong place, after all.

00:21:23.750 --> 00:21:25.220
Could it be...

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:31.090
It appears to be functional.

00:21:31.090 --> 00:21:32.610
Huh? What's that mean?

00:21:32.610 --> 00:21:33.830
Is this a bus, too?

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:35.330
On the ocean...

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:39.230
Serval-chan.

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:43.450
I want to go beyond the ocean 
to search for humans.

00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:45.030
Beyond the ocean?

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:46.520
Does that mean...

00:23:18.440 --> 00:23:24.620
Raccoon-san was so startled by the eruption 
that she fell off the cliff, she said.

00:23:24.620 --> 00:23:30.130
That was when I saw it! 
A black shadow made off with my hat!

00:23:30.130 --> 00:23:33.320
A black shadow... Intriguing...

00:23:33.320 --> 00:23:36.380
Does that sound like it could be useful 
for your new work, Sensei?!

00:23:36.380 --> 00:23:41.390
Huh? Could it have been a Friend 
who was born from the eruption?

00:23:41.780 --> 00:23:43.330
PPP Preview!

00:23:43.330 --> 00:23:45.350
This week, we're learning 
about the brown bear.

00:23:45.350 --> 00:23:47.120
I guess they hate the smell of snakes.

00:23:47.120 --> 00:23:47.690
What kind of smell is that?

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:49.170
But I bet they'd be delicious cooked, right?

00:23:49.170 --> 00:23:50.780
Emperor, what the heck are you?!

00:23:50.780 --> 00:23:52.930
I am a god. No, that's not right.

00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:56.370
Next time: "Cerulean."
